This is a tutorial of Ariadne Numeric, written as a simple self-contained example (SSCE).
It is intentionally built as a standalone project and assumes that the ariadne-numeric library has already been installed.

To compile and run the tutorial:

1. mkdir build
2. cd build
3. cmake ..
4. cmake --build .
5. ./tutorial_numeric

If Ariadne Numeric was installed to a non-standard prefix, pass it when configuring:

    cmake .. -DCMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/path/to/ariadne-numeric/install

On a multi-config generator such as Visual Studio, build and run the Release configuration:

    cmake --build . --config Release
    .\Release\tutorial_numeric.exe
